prompt:
In web/src/views/tasks.ts, function renderTasks shows the project settings panel at the top of a project's task list with `${renderProjectPanel(project!, { machines: ..., assets: ..., dev: ..., pick: ..., thumb, })}`. Show the PROJ-OVERVIEW Overview there instead, with that same panel inside its collapsed Settings section:
1. Add the import `import { renderOverview, accessCount, type SectionName } from "./overview";` after the renderProjectPanel import.
2. Replace the expression `${renderProjectPanel(project!, { ...the same options... })}` with `${renderOverview({ project: project!, o: s.overviews[project!.id], editing: s.overviewEditing === project!.id, more: s.overviewMore.has(project!.id), activityAll: s.overviewActivityAll.has(project!.id), preview: s.overviewPreview !== undefined, open: (sec) => s.overviewOpen[`${project!.id}:${sec}`] ?? openByDefault(sec, s.overviews[project!.id]) }, renderProjectPanel(project!, { ...the same options, unchanged... }))}`.
3. Add this function above renderTasks:
/** PROJ-OVERVIEW: sections open on a desktop and closed on a phone; Settings starts closed, Access when it has more than 3 items. */
function openByDefault(sec: SectionName, o: ProjectOverview | undefined): boolean {
  if (sec === "settings" || window.matchMedia("(max-width: 760px)").matches) return false;
  return sec !== "access" || (accessCount(o) ?? 0) <= 3;
}
and add ProjectOverview to the existing type import from "../api/types" (or a new `import type { ProjectOverview } from "../api/types";`). Change nothing else.
